WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.281
Atoll ecology is a paradox: some of the richest ecosystems on Earth sit beside some of

00:00:05.281 --> 00:00:05.969
the poorest.

00:00:07.069 --> 00:00:11.872
In the sea, coral reefs are among the most productive ecosystems on the planet.

00:00:11.872 --> 00:00:14.547
On land, soils are thin, salty and alkaline,

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:17.465
and the native flora is small and widely spread,

00:00:17.465 --> 00:00:20.688
joined by coconut and breadfruit brought by voyagers.

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:23.665
The reef is a sediment factory.

00:00:23.665 --> 00:00:26.934
If corals bleach, or if the ocean becomes more acidic,

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:30.930
the supply of sand and gravel that keeps islands alive slows down.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.351
So threats to reefs are threats to land.

00:00:34.451 --> 00:00:39.823
On the uninhabited western islets, the Funafuti Conservation Area, set up in 1996,

00:00:39.823 --> 00:00:43.556
protects seabird roosts and green turtle nesting beaches,

00:00:43.556 --> 00:00:45.980
and the reefs and lagoon around them.
